('baseCost','共有 (n−1)(n−2)/2 个切法，每次读 n 位，基线做 O(n³) 次逐位更新。n=30000 时已有 449955001 个切法。下面的小输入基线用于核对，不能用于最大输入。Python 整数可增长到 O(n) 位；大整数运算并非常数成本，所以真实位运算成本还会更高。','There are (n−1)(n−2)/2 cuts, each reading n bits: O(n³) digit updates in the baseline. At n=30000 there are already 449955001 cuts. This small-input baseline is a checking tool, not a maximum-input solution. Python integers can grow to O(n) bits, so big-integer operations add further bit-level cost.'),
('baselineTitle','查看独立基线 Python','Inspect independent baseline Python'),
('baseRead','value 的循环实现“旧值乘 2 加下一位”；切片右端不包含在内。双循环恰好遍历所有非空三段，发现任意答案就返回。它不依赖后面的首个 1 推导。','The value loop implements “double then add the bit”; slice right endpoints are excluded. The nested loops cover every nonempty three-part split and return any valid one. This method does not depend on the first-one argument below.'),
('p2','这一步要回答：为什么末尾能决定切在哪里？去掉前导零后，从首个 1 到该段末尾的数字叫有效串。非零二进制数的有效串唯一，因此三个相等的值必有完全相同的有效串，也必有相同数量的 1。','Why can the end determine the cuts? After leading zeros are removed, the digits from the first 1 to the end form the significant string. A nonzero binary value has a unique significant string. Equal values must therefore have identical significant strings, including equal counts of ones.'),
('countDerive','先数整个数组的 1，记为 ones。如果 ones=0，任意三段都是零，可返回 [0,2]。否则 ones 必须能被 3 整除；每段恰有 k=ones/3 个 1。按顺序，第 1、k+1、2k+1 个 1 就分别是三段首个 1 的下标 s1、s2、s3。','First count the ones in the whole array as ones. If ones=0, every part is zero and [0,2] works. Otherwise ones must be divisible by 3, with k=ones/3 ones per part. In order, ones number 1, k+1, and 2k+1 give the first-one indices s1, s2, and s3.'),
('lengthDerive','对 10101，ones=3，k=1，三个首位是 s1=0、s2=2、s3=4。第三段必须一直用到数组末尾，所以它的有效串是 arr[4..4]=1，长度 L=n−s3=1。前两段也各需长 1 的有效串；剩下的间隔零留给下一段作为前导零。于是 i=s1+L−1=0，j=s2+L=3。','For 10101, ones=3 and k=1, so s1=0, s2=2, s3=4. Part 3 must reach the array end. Its significant string is arr[4..4]=1, of length L=n−s3=1. Each earlier significant string also needs length 1. Unused gap zeros become leading zeros of the next part. Thus i=s1+L−1=0 and j=s2+L=3.'),
('complication','只增加尾零来检验这个结论：100100100 的首位为 0、3、6，L=3。三个有效串都必须是 100，答案为 [2,6]。但 1010100 的首位为 0、2、4，L=3，第一段需占到下标 2，已经碰到第二段的首个 1，空间不够。','Test the effect of trailing zeros: 100100100 has starts 0,3,6 and L=3. All three significant strings must be 100, giving [2,6]. But 1010100 has starts 0,2,4 and L=3: part 1 would need index 2, which already holds part 2’s first 1. There is not enough space.'),
('formula','L = n − s3；s1 + L ≤ s2 且 s2 + L ≤ s3；对每个 d∈[0,L)：arr[s1+d] = arr[s2+d] = arr[s3+d]','L = n − s3; s1 + L ≤ s2 and s2 + L ≤ s3; for each d∈[0,L): arr[s1+d] = arr[s2+d] = arr[s3+d]'),
('wrong','诱人的错误：只要 1 的总数能被 3 整除就成功。反例 110101101 有 6 个 1，但首位 0、3、6 对应的三个长 3 串为 110、101、101。1 的数量相同，数值却是 6、5、5。尾零是否够放、内部数字是否一致，都还要检查。','Tempting mistake: a count divisible by 3 is enough. Counterexample 110101101 has 6 ones, but starts 0,3,6 give length-3 strings 110,101,101, worth 6,5,5. Equal one counts are insufficient. We still need room for the trailing zeros and identical internal digits.'),
('invariant','不变量是每次比较之前仍成立的事实：已经检查的 d 列在三个有效串中全部相同。起初 d=0，还没检查任何列；比较下一列，相同就把已确认前缀延长一位，不同就立即无解，因为首位和长度都无法更换。检查满 L 列便得到相同的完整有效串。','An invariant is a fact that remains true before each comparison: all d columns already checked are equal across the three significant strings. Initially d=0, so no columns have been checked. An equal next column extends the confirmed prefix by one bit. A different column proves failure because the starts and length cannot change. After L equal columns, the full significant strings match.'),
('proof','充分性：两个空间条件保证前两段的有效串不重叠下一首位；每组的 k 个 1 都在对应串内。间隔不可能还有 1，因此只会成为下一段的前导零。返回的三段非空且值相同。必要性：任何非零答案必须分到相同数量的 1，因而有同样的 s1、s2、s3 和 L；空间或任一列失败都排除了全部答案。','Sufficiency: the two gap conditions keep each earlier significant string from overlapping the next start. Each group’s k ones lies in its corresponding string; there can be no extra 1 in a gap, so gaps become leading zeros of the next part. The returned parts are nonempty and equal. Necessity: every nonzero solution has equal one counts, forcing the same s1,s2,s3 and L. A failed gap or column therefore rules out every solution.'),
('sim','这是浏览器教学模拟，不执行下方 Python。只展示小预设的完整检查过程；保留的历史额外占空间，不能算作提交算法的空间。数字是原输入，下标标在数字下方。','This is a browser teaching simulation; it does not execute the Python below. It shows the full checking process for small presets. Stored history uses extra memory, separate from submission space. Digits are the original input; indices appear below them.'),
